/* Magic Camera — English (development language).

   Identity mappings. They exist so the key set is written down in one place and
   a test can hold the translations to it: without an English file, a typo in a
   `Text("…")` literal silently becomes a new untranslated key that shows up in
   English on a Czech phone and nothing fails.

   SwiftUI uses the literal itself as the lookup key, so a string only becomes
   localisable by being a single literal. `Text("a" + "b")` is not one — keep
   sentences whole even when they are long. */

